[17592186096847 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1045 "Integration Using the Double-Angle Formulas" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1050 1380.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096847 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8fcbc060-700b-5d19-b54b-f889d83b8904" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097508 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097508 #edb/ref 1061 637993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097508 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "65464d10-225f-54ed-8f6c-218e4b4d2657" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097508 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097509 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097509 #edb/ref 1061 637994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097509 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "31f4b71b-4658-5674-ba5b-63ad1748c1a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097509 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097510 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097510 #edb/ref 1061 637997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097510 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de91749b-079a-5aad-bc6d-d965d5964042" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097510 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097511 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097511 #edb/ref 1061 638001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097511 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "64d8b65c-b5fa-5e7e-90a8-fb3e529eddf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097511 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097512 #edb/ref 1061 638004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097512 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cae0f96e-fc14-5c8f-ab39-3411f5328c23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097512 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097513 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097513 #edb/ref 1061 637998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097513 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ed8cffe0-39e4-5348-a88e-8324d086d5f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097513 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097922 #edb/ref 1064 "How can we calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x?$  \n\nNotice that we have the product of sine and cosine with the same argument $(x).$ In such cases, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve the integral.\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for sine, which is\n\n$$\n\\sin {2x}=2\\sin x \\cos x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\sin x \\cos x =  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin {2x}.\n$$\n\nPlugging this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {2x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{4} \\cos {2x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nIn general, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve any integral that's of the form \n\n$$\n\\int \\sin\\left(ax+b\\right)\\cos(ax+b)\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n Let's take a look at another example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097922 #edb/ref 1065 878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097922 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c1eb8ee2-db04-591c-b7f9-cd699c4e3573" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097922 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097923 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's recall the three double-angle formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the double-angle formulas for cosine to integrate $\\sin^2{x}$ and $\\cos^2{x}.$ Let's take a look at some examples." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097923 #edb/ref 1065 880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097923 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "87755d89-cab8-5737-9e44-ae816aefe23f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097923 #edb/ref 1067 "Using the Double-Angle Formulas for Cosine" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247457 #edb/ref 1080 "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247457 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247457 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "049104f3-f0f9-54a7-b34b-435d0972bf29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248897 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248897 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248897 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4eaf12f-fe73-5186-a4a3-9f8f03675c77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248926 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248926 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248926 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8ff8b54-32a2-5896-b5ee-9f76878d8456" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249110 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-2x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249110 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249110 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bdae4aa9-7adc-544f-8974-b9d6969f616e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249118 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249118 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249118 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "beaa505f-9480-5438-ad07-7fb3d61dda35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249967 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186247457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249967 