ed}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526034 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526034 #edb/ref 1069 "q-347204" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526034 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526034 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c9/c91e196377aad64db49224cb5e38c1c8336171649708ec78b9cb80ebe6803128.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=-3{cos}^{2}⁡x+3{sin}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}+3,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526034 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6c56b3c3-015d-5836-a8b0-fb20b975ad9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526034 #edb/ref 1074 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(-3{cos}^{2}⁡x+3{sin}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=-3{cos}^{2}⁡x+3{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(-3{cos}^{2}⁡x+3{sin}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )+\\frac{(-\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+3(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}+\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-(-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{12}+3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526048 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526048 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526048 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526048 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/28/28be65f566e93427105af6c87c46fa51f1a473363247f35a4aa481b93dc70090.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.$ The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526048 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "85abb599-4be2-577d-9d0b-59402cc7e2bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526048 #edb/ref 1074 "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{2}$ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))={sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3[(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}))-(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))] \\\\  & =3[(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}-1)-(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1)] \\\\  & =3(2\\pi ) \\\\  & =6\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526110 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186526117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526110 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22c9038a-77de-5265-acd7-65600a8a79a2" #edb/ref 175921860454